   "ply": 9,
   "t": 630.5,
   "fen": "rn1qk1nr/pbpp1ppp/1p2p3/8/1b1PP3/2NB4/PPP1NPPP/R1BQK2R b KQkq - 5 5",
   "line": [
    "Ne2"
   ],
   "spoken": "The whole reason for the knight on e2 rather than f3: with it on f3, Black plays d5 and starts leaning on the knight — an annoying pressure the e2 setup avoids, so after the knight to f6 we simply castle.",
